{
 "schema": "br-6r7k2 acceptance v1",
 "bead": "br-6r7k2",
 "author": "CopperGoose (Claude Opus 5.5)",
 "claim_under_test": "5f577775 (+ ac929af8, 4625eb9b): the WBQ durability latch clears in-process once the failed write-back is reconciled; that commit made no runtime ENOSPC/HTTP acceptance claim",
 "rule": "br-6r7k2 acceptance probe (written 2026-10-18 ~14:45Z, before the probe script ran even once).\n\nClaim under test: Jeff's 5f577775 (+ ac929af8, 4625eb9b) clears the WBQ durability latch in-process once the failed\nwrite-back is reconciled. 5f577775 says \"no runtime ENOSPC/HTTP acceptance claim\"; this is that acceptance run.\nBead done-when: \"arm the latch with a simulated ENOSPC on one archive write, restore the disk, and then, without a\nrestart, sends succeed within about 2 min. The missing archive file is written, and /health/durability returns to\nhealthy.\"\n\nArms: B = main ac0dcbcd portable release (build34, contains all three commits). A = shipped v0.3.38 image binary\n(no in-process clear) = planted negative: the same probe must FAIL on A, or the probe cannot detect the defect.\nOrder A then B. Host lock held.\n\nSetup per arm: ghcr v0.3.38 image (B: build34 mcp-agent-mail bind-mounted over /usr/local/bin/mcp-agent-mail),\narchive STORAGE_ROOT=/data/mailbox on a 32 MB tmpfs at /data, database on a host bind mount\n(DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////db/storage.sqlite3), disk thresholds scaled to the tmpfs (fatal 1 MB, critical 2, warning 3;\ncheck interval default 60 s), bearer token, HTTP over a published loopback port.\n\nSteps: 3 warm-up sends must succeed and be archived. Fill /data with a zero filler outside STORAGE_ROOT until ENOSPC,\nthen send message M at once. Precondition ARMED: within 300 s /health/durability reports allows_writes=false with\nwrite_gate DURABILITY_DEGRADED. Then restore space by remounting /data at 256 MB (no file is removed). Poll health\nevery 5 s and try one send every 15 s for 600 s.\n\nDecision per arm:\n  NOT ARMED: precondition fails -> INCONCLUSIVE for that arm (reported; no claim).\n  PASS: without a server restart (same container start time, RestartCount 0, same server pid), within 180 s of the\n    remount: a send succeeds, M's archive file exists, and /health/durability shows allows_writes=true with no\n    write_gate.\n  FAIL: ARMED but PASS not met within 600 s.\nbr-6r7k2 closes (citing 5f577775 and this run) only if B PASSES and A FAILS. If B passes in 180..600 s, it is a FAIL\nunder this rule (the bead asks about 2 min), reported with the time. The unrepairable-case acceptance (\"latch stays\nwhen the reconcile cannot repair\") is NOT exercised here; it rests on 5f577775's unit tests and is stated as such.\nThe guidance-text half of the bead (refusal + /health say only `am doctor repair`) is separate work.\n\nAmendment 2026-10-18 14:44Z, while A runs and before B starts, after seeing A's live /health/durability: v0.3.38's\nhealth has no write_gate field (main added it in apply_wbq_write_gate), and its degraded_read_only state there comes\nfrom disk pressure, not the latch. So the script's ARMED check cannot fire on A. A's server log shows the latch armed\n0.3 s after the fill (\"[wbq-drain] op failed after retries ... refusing further writes\"). For A only, ARMED is judged\nbehaviourally from the recorded events: a send refused with DURABILITY_DEGRADED. A's planted-negative FAIL then means\nevery after-restore send in the 600 s window is refused with DURABILITY_DEGRADED. B's precondition, PASS criteria\nand script are unchanged.\n\nAddendum 2026-10-18 15:00Z, after A and B ran, adding a STRICTER requirement (nothing relaxed): B's disk was full\nfor only ~8 s, so the 60 s disk sampler never recorded critical/fatal pressure, and seed_retries skips while pressure\nis critical. The studio outage held the disk full for an hour or more. B2 = B with the full disk held 300 s after\nARMED (as A effectively was) before the remount. Same PASS criteria (<= 180 s after the remount, no restart). br-6r7k2\ncloses only if B PASS, B2 PASS and A FAIL.\n",
 "binaries": {
  "A": "ghcr.io/dicklesworthstone/mcp_agent_mail_rust:v0.3.38 image binary (revision f9c68b4e)",
  "B_and_B2": {
